---
layout: base.njk
title: Demo
description: "Click through Prospektor's real screens, one lit at a time with one sentence each, without an account. Pick a chapter and press Next."
# One page per language (#535) — see src/index.njk for the reasoning. The
# chrome is this site's and goes through the catalogues; each step's title and
# sentence are the studio's, in the language it holds them in, and fall back
# to English the way a help guide's title does.
pagination:
  data: languages
  size: 1
  alias: language
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ language.prefix }}/demo/"
---

{#- #767, 28 Sep 2026. The operator: *"We should also have a clickable demo
    like this: https://app.storylane.io/share/7dnsrqniygbj"*. Reevo's demo is
    a title card, three chapters to pick from, then the real product greyed
    with one element lit and one sentence per screen, Next.

    Nothing on this page is written here. Every screen, every ring and every
    sentence is the studio's one-minute tour (`TOUR_STEPS`, reshaped by #766
    into Find, Engage and Teach), read off the real product by
    `npm run demo:capture` into data/demo.json and src/assets/img/demo/. So
    the demo cannot say a sentence the tour does not, and test/demo.test.js
    goes red the day the strings snapshot stops holding one of them.

    Less is more, applied: no wall of chapters and no paragraph of preamble.
    One h1, then the first screen with its one card, which is the tour's own
    opening card and already the three chapters to pick from. Every step is
    one figure: the screen, the lit element (a link that is also Next), and
    the card below it with the count, the title, the sentence and Back/Next.
    demo.js shows one figure at a time and drives the hash; with no script
    the ten figures stand in order and every link still lands.

    The card sits BELOW the screen rather than over it, on purpose: the rings
    are mostly the right-hand panel of the screen, so a card over the screen
    would cover what it points at, and a card below scales down to a phone
    without covering anything.

    The end card is the free scan, which is this site's *Book a live demo*
    (ROADMAP.md #766): a stranger gets a real result on their own domain
    where Reevo shows somebody else's. -#}

{%- set total = demo.steps | length -%}

<header class="page-hero demo-hero">
  <div class="page-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">{% t %}the demo{% endt %}</span>
    <h1 class="page-h1">{% t %}The real screens, no account.{% endt %}</h1>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="demo">
  <div class="demo-stage" id="demoStage" data-total="{{ total }}">
    {%- for step in demo.steps %}
    {%- set next = 'step-' + (step.n + 1) if not loop.last else 'demo-end' %}
    {%- set chapter = demo.chapterNames[step.chapter] if step.chapter else null %}
    <figure class="demo-step" id="step-{{ step.n }}" data-n="{{ step.n }}"{% if step.chapter %} data-chapter="{{ step.chapter }}"{% endif %}>
      <div class="demo-shot">
        <img src="{{ step.image | asset }}" width="{{ demo.viewport.width }}" height="{{ demo.viewport.height }}" alt="{{ step.title[language.code] or step.title.en }}"{% if not loop.first %} loading="lazy"{% endif %}>
        {%- if step.ring %}
        {#- The lit element. A link, so it is the press that moves the walk
            on, with or without demo.js; the dimming around it is its own
            box-shadow, so the screen needs no second layer. -#}
        <a class="demo-ring" href="#{{ next }}" aria-label="{{ 'Next' | t }}"
           style="left:{{ step.ring.x * 100 }}%;top:{{ step.ring.y * 100 }}%;width:{{ step.ring.w * 100 }}%;height:{{ step.ring.h * 100 }}%"></a>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
      <figcaption class="demo-card">
        <div class="demo-card-text">
          <p class="demo-count">{% if chapter %}<span class="demo-chapter {{ step.chapter }}">{{ chapter[language.code] or chapter.en }}</span> · {% endif %}{{ 'Step {n} of {total}' | t({ n: step.n, total: total }) }}</p>
          <h2>{{ step.title[language.code] or step.title.en }}</h2>
          <p>{{ step.body[language.code] or step.body.en }}</p>
          {%- if loop.first and demo.chapters | length %}
          {#- The tour's opening card is the three verbs to pick from (#766);
              each lands on its chapter's first step. -#}
          {#- A div, not a <nav>: main.css fixes every <nav> to the top of the
              page, because the header is the only one it expected. -#}
          <div class="demo-chapters" role="group" aria-label="{{ step.title[language.code] or step.title.en }}">
            {%- for c in demo.chapters %}
            <a class="demo-chapter-btn {{ c.id }}" href="#step-{{ c.first }}" data-chapter="{{ c.id }}">{{ c.name[language.code] or c.name.en }}</a>
            {%- endfor %}
          </div>
          {%- endif %}
        </div>
        <div class="demo-actions">
          <ol class="demo-dots" aria-hidden="true">
            {%- for k in range(1, total + 1) %}<li{% if k == step.n %} class="is-on"{% endif %}></li>{% endfor %}
          </ol>
          {%- if not loop.first %}
          <a class="btn-ghost demo-back" href="#step-{{ step.n - 1 }}">{% t %}Back{% endt %}</a>
          {%- endif %}
          <a class="demo-next" href="#{{ next }}">{% t %}Next{% endt %}</a>
        </div>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    {%- endfor %}

    {#- The way out is the free scan: their own domain, a real result, no
        sign-up. One primary action, and Back. -#}
    <div class="demo-step demo-end" id="demo-end">
      <h2>{% t %}Now on your own site.{% endt %}</h2>
      <p>{% t %}The scan reads your site and shows you who it would go after, in about thirty seconds. No sign-up.{% endt %}</p>
      <div class="demo-end-actions">
        <a class="btn-cta" href="{{ '/#scan' | localize }}">{% t %}Scan your site for free{% endt %}</a>
        {%- if total %}
        <a class="btn-ghost demo-back" href="#step-{{ total }}">{% t %}Back{% endt %}</a>
        {%- endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{#- defer (#137): an IIFE that looks its stage up by id and returns if it is
    absent; with the DOM complete it hides every figure but the current one. -#}
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/demo.js' | asset }}" defer></script>
